  "heat": 3,
  "text": "Rahab ran a safe house and negotiated her family out of a war. Joshua chapter two. Two spies come into Jericho and lodge at the house of a harlot named Rahab. The king hears about it and sends word to bring them out. And Rahab hides them under stalks of flax on her roof, then tells the messengers the men have already left and if they hurry they will catch them. The text records what she said, plainly, without softening it. Then she goes up to the roof and tells the spies the real reason. We have heard what your God did at the Red Sea. Our hearts did melt. The Lord your God, he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath. So she cuts a deal, and notice she does not negotiate for herself alone. Save my father, and my mother, and my brethren, and my sisters, and all that they have. They tell her to bind a line of scarlet thread in the window. Her house is on the town wall, and she lets them down by a cord. Jericho falls and her whole household lives. And Matthew's genealogy puts her in the family line of Jesus.",
